
The following instructions allow to reproduce the bytecode of the Etheria contract 0xe414716f017b5c1457bf98e985bccb135dff81f2.  


1. Upload the 3 solidity files included in the .tar.gz into Remix (17584309.sol, 21498383.sol, etheria.sol).

   Note 1: The filenames and contents (including comments, line breaks and whitespace) should not be altered. 
           Please _upload_ the files (instead of copy/pasting) to ensure that the files are not altered in any way.
   Note 2: The files should be placed in the _root_ of the workspace (_not_ under contracts/).

2. Select compiler 0.1.6+commit.d41f8b7c

3. Check "Enable optimization"

4. Compile the 2 auxiliary files in the following order
  - 17584309.sol
  - 21498383.sol
  
5. Finally compile the contract's source: etheria.sol

   This should produce the exact bytecode of 0xe414716f017b5c1457bf98e985bccb135dff81f2.


Note that the 2 auxiliary files are trivial contracts completely unrelated to Etheria. The needed
simply because soljson-v0.1.6+commit.d41f8b7c.js has non-deterministic output, which depends on
_previous_ compilation. Compiling these 2 auxiliary contracts (which were found via random search)
just happens to leave the compiler in the state needed to produce the exact target bytecode.
